# Research Gap Analysis

## Gap 1: Limited Generalisation of Single-Representation Detection
Current AI-based vulnerability detection approaches predominantly rely on a single representation of smart contract code — source code, opcode sequences, or control-flow graphs — limiting their ability to capture the full semantic complexity of contracts.

## Gap 2: Fragmented Multi-Layer Security Solutions
Blockchain security research is fragmented, with studies focusing on individual threats in isolation.

## Positioning of This Research
This research addresses both gaps by:
1. Proposing a multimodal deep learning prototype that integrates source code, opcode sequences, and control-flow graphs.
2. Positioning smart contract security within a broader multi-layer blockchain security context.
